# Client Features - Complete Reference

## Pages & Routes

### 1. Login Page (`/login`)
- Firebase email/password authentication
- Redirects to home after successful login
- Auto-redirects to home if already authenticated

### 2. My Library / Clips Page (`/`)
**Main clip browsing interface**

Features:
- Grid and grouped view modes (toggle with 'L' key)
- Pagination with infinite scroll support
- Batch selection mode (Ctrl+A to select all, Shift+Click for range)
- Filters:
  - Game filter
  - Search by filename/displayName/tags
  - Published/unpublished filter
  - Starred filter
  - Tag filter (multiple tags, AND logic)
- Drag and drop file import
- Batch operations (see Batch Operations section)

### 3. Today's Clips Page (`/today`)
**Carousel view of clips created today**

Features:
- Full-screen carousel with embla-carousel
- Thumbnail strip navigation
- Auto-play video on slide change
- Inline rename and delete
- Smooth animations and transitions

### 4. Collection Page (`/collections/:id`)
**View clips within a specific collection**

Features:
- Same filtering as main library (inherited from clips store)
- Remove clips from collection
- Infinite scroll pagination
- Grid/grouped view modes
- Empty state when no clips

### 5. Clip Detail Page (`/clips/:id`)
**Detailed view of a single clip**

Features:
- Large video player with controls
- Clip metadata display (size, date, resolution, codec, fps)
- Notes editor (markdown support)
- Tags management
- Collections management (add/remove from collections)
- Publishing controls
- Action menu with all clip operations

### 6. Trim Page (`/trim/:id`)
**Video trimming interface**

Features:
- Visual timeline with frame strip preview
- Drag handles to set start/end points
- Real-time length calculation
- Video preview with current selection
- Save to create new trimmed version (replaces original)

### 7. Advanced Editor Page (`/editor`)
**Multi-clip video editor**

Features:
- Clip library panel (toggle with button)
- Timeline with multiple clips support
- Video preview area
- Properties panel for selected clip (toggle with button)
- Clip operations:
  - Drag clips to timeline
  - Trim clips on timeline
  - Adjust volume per clip
  - Mute/unmute clips
  - Remove clips
  - Reorder clips (drag to move)
- Zoom controls (in/out)
- Playback controls (play/pause, skip forward/backward)
- Export compiled video
- Progress tracking during export
- Keyboard shortcuts (Space, Left/Right arrows, Delete)

### 8. Tag Patterns Page (`/tag-patterns`)
**Manage smart tag suggestions**

Features:
- Add/edit/delete tag patterns
- Pattern categories: General, Gameplay, Weapons, Maps, Modes, Quality
- Regex pattern support
- Filter by category
- Search patterns
- Pattern preview with regex source display

### 9. Statistics Page (`/stats`)
**Analytics and insights**

Features:
- Stat cards:
  - Total clips count
  - Storage used (total + average)
  - Published clips count & percentage
  - Starred clips count & percentage
- Games list with clip counts and stats per game
- Most used tags list
- Activity chart (last 14 days)
- Quick filter links (click published/starred to filter main library)

### 10. Settings Page (`/settings`)
**User preferences configuration**

Features:
- **General Settings**:
  - Default view mode (grid/grouped)
  - Date format (relative/absolute)
  - Show clip metadata toggle
  - Compact mode toggle
  - Items per page (10/25/50/100/200)
  - Confirm before delete toggle

- **Playback Settings**:
  - Auto-play on hover toggle
  - Mute videos by default toggle

- **Advanced Settings**:
  - Enable keyboard shortcuts toggle
  - Keyboard shortcuts reference guide

- **Settings Management**:
  - Export settings to JSON
  - Import settings from JSON
  - Reset to defaults

## Shell Layout Features

The shell layout wraps all authenticated pages and provides:

### Header
- App branding and logo
- Page title and subtitle (dynamic per route)
- Search bar with real-time filtering
- Global actions (file import, scan)
- User menu with logout

### Sidebar
- Navigation links:
  - My Library
  - Today's Clips
  - Tag Patterns
  - Statistics
  - Settings
- Games list with clip counts (clickable to filter)
- Collections list:
  - Create new collection
  - Edit collection name
  - Delete collection
  - Click to view collection
- Expandable sections (show more/less)
- Drag and drop support to add clips to collections

### Main Content Area
- Scrollable content
- Consistent padding and styling

## Keyboard Shortcuts

Global shortcuts (when enabled in settings):
- `G` - Go to Library
- `S` - Go to Settings
- `/` - Focus search bar
- `Escape` - Cancel/close dialogs, exit selection mode

Clips page shortcuts:
- `L` - Toggle view mode (grid/list)
- `Space` - Load more clips
- `↑` - Scroll up
- `↓` - Scroll down
- `Ctrl+A` - Select all clips (enters selection mode)

Editor shortcuts:
- `Space` - Play/pause
- `←` - Skip backward
- `→` - Skip forward
- `Delete` - Delete selected clip from timeline

Trim page:
- Video player controls (standard)

## PWA Features

- Installable as Progressive Web App
- Service worker for offline support
- App manifest with icons for all platforms:
  - Android launcher icons
  - iOS app icons
  - Windows 11 tiles
- Push notification support (infrastructure ready)

